          "body": "Closes #419.\n\nWhen a historical-thread client disconnects, replay now stops before starting further repository work. A pending operation may settle, but a late rejection does not attempt an error response on the closed connection. Normal completed GETs, connected error policy, current-thread reads and historical response bytes retain their behavior; the response-close listener is removed on settlement.\n\nGPT-6.1 Sol xhigh implemented the fix. Separate GPT-6.1 Sol xhigh behavior QA reproduced the defect on actual integrated main and verified the candidate through compiled production routes over TCP and file SQLite. All eight disconnect cases stop new calls/writes, eleven connected success responses match the baseline byte for byte, and ten negative controls preserve their outcomes. The fixture uses controlled promise gates and synthetic histories; it does not claim ordinary gateway or browser behavior. Actual process/stream exit and independent PID/listener readbacks confirm owned cleanup. [Baseline](docs/qa/2026-11-15-history-disconnect-baseline/README.md) · [Candidate QA](docs/qa/2026-11-15-history-disconnect-candidate/README.md)\n\nThe final regression test produced seven expected disconnect failures and three passing controls on old source; all 22 focused tests passed on the candidate. Types, scoped lint, formatting and diff checks passed. The initial fixture draft failed and remains separately recorded. Full local API coverage failed on an unchanged Windows reset-test setup rename (`EPERM`): 1,952 passed, 14 skipped, one failed, with no coverage totals. The unchanged isolated reset test passed 7/7; [#489](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/issues/489) tracks the unexplained failure. Current-head full CI must still establish every coverage floor. [Implementation evidence](docs/qa/2026-11-15-history-disconnect-implementation/README.md)\n\nCurrent-head CI, Claude Opus 5.5 xhigh opposite-family scan 1 and fresh independent Astra max final audit remain pending under the shared three-scan cap. No owner acceptance or overall intent completion is claimed. This PR also archives the already completed #410 CI/review/merge record; that changes no product source. The owner instance and separate PR #460 merge hold remain untouched. [Delivery register](docs/delivery/2026-11-13-four-intents-register.md)\n",
